# Observability & Doctor

## Diagnostics (TUI base layer)

TUI mode always logs to `.ralph/diagnostics/logs/ralph-{timestamp}.log` (last 5 kept automatically).

```bash
RALPH_DIAGNOSTICS=1 ralph run -p "your prompt"
```

Output in `.ralph/diagnostics/<timestamp>/`:
- `agent-output.jsonl` — Agent text, tool calls, results
- `orchestration.jsonl` — Hat selection, events, backpressure
- `errors.jsonl` — Parse errors, validation failures

```bash
jq 'select(.type == "tool_call")' .ralph/diagnostics/*/agent-output.jsonl
ralph clean --diagnostics
```

## Runtime Diagnosis (U0-U8, observability + self-calibration layer)

Above TUI / full diagnostics. Drops back-pressure points (payload / execution contract, workflow guard, stall, loop stale) to `recovery.jsonl`. When U5 drift detector's 3 metrics (field completeness / coord join rate / emit cadence) fall below threshold → `drift.jsonl`. On loop termination, appends `## Diagnostics` section to `.ralph/agent/summary.md` and writes `diagnosis-summary.json` seed.

- **Enable (env preferred)**: `RALPH_DIAGNOSTICS=1 ralph run -c ralph.yml -H builtin:<preset> -p "..."`. Disk-only mode (no prompt alert): set `telemetry.runtime_diagnosis: { enabled: true, write_artifacts: true, prompt_injection_enabled: true, ... }` in `ralph.yml`.
- **Report**: `ralph diagnose --session latest` (Markdown) or `--format json` (CI, `schema_version="1"`); `--diagnostics-root` overrides default root.
- **Exit codes**: `0` rendered / `2` no session / `3` invalid path / `4` I/O failure.
- **Recovery count (2026-06-17-004 U4)**: `diagnosis-summary.json`'s `recovery_count` now aggregates workspace-level `<root>/.ralph/recovery.jsonl` (CLI emit rejections) AND session-level `<root>/.ralph/diagnostics/<id>/recovery.jsonl` (hard gate / workflow guard) — two journals; `notes` lists both paths. `ralph diagnose` falls back to workspace journal when session journal is empty, avoiding stale session hiding cli_emit rejections.

Full reference: `docs/guide/runtime-diagnosis.md` (config matrix, report fields, common symptom troubleshooting, disk file manifest).

## Doctor — Plan Frontmatter Drift Detection

`ralph doctor plan-sync [--plan PATH]` (2026-06-17-004 U5 / R7) detects inconsistency between plan YAML frontmatter `status` and `.ralph/agent/tasks.jsonl` closure state:

- `status: completed` but `open` task remains → fail
- `status: stalled-after-uN` but uN all `closed` and no open → fail
- `status` not in allowed enum (`draft / active / stalled-after-u0..8 / uN-closed-u(N+1)-pending / completed / abandoned`) → fail
- Missing `tasks.jsonl` → warning only, not fail
- Without `--plan`, auto-picks the most recent `mtime` `.md` under `docs/plans/` or `docs/achieved/plan/`
- `ce-executor-serial` preset coordinator instructions include HARD RULE: every `work.done` MUST update plan frontmatter `status` (after `ralph tools task close`, before `ralph emit work.ready`)

**8 envelope sources**: `stall_recovery / missing_event_gate / workflow_guard / execution_contract / payload_contract / drift_monitor / hook_retry / loop_stale`
**6 outcomes**: `pending / recovered / repeated / escalated / failed / not_retriable`
**Responder 3-tier escalation**: Soft (prompt alert) → Hard (`task.resume` to safe target) → Final (`TerminationHint`, NOT overriding `PayloadContractViolation`)
